  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The 8(a) Business Development set-aside program obligated $205M in FY2027 to date across 822 awards, with an average award size of $250K. Obligations fell 98.0% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is partial; prior full-year obligations were $12.3B in FY22, $14.3B in FY23, $15.4B in FY24, $14.1B in FY25, and $10.5B in FY26. The Department of Homeland Security led FY2027 to date buying with $59.8M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $36.5M and the Department of Transportation with $18.9M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry for FY2027 to date with $33.3M, followed by Janitorial Services with $20.9M and Facilities Support Services with $18.2M. T47 INTERNATIONAL, INC. is the largest vendor for FY2027 to date with $18.7M, followed by BERING STRAITS PROFESSIONAL SERVICES, LLC with $12.3M and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC with $11.4M. The FY2027 to date figures reflect a sharp drop from recent full fiscal years and represent fiscal year to date activity only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is FY2027 to date 8(a) activity?",
        "body": "The federal government obligated $205M through 8(a) set-asides in FY2027 to date across 822 awards, with an average award size of $250K. Obligations fell 98.0% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is partial and follows five prior full fiscal years of higher totals, the largest being $15.4B in FY24."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers, vendors, and industries so far this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security led buying with $59.8M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $36.5M and the Department of Transportation with $18.9M. T47 INTERNATIONAL, INC. is the top vendor with $18.7M, followed by BERING STRAITS PROFESSIONAL SERVICES, LLC with $12.3M and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC with $11.4M. Computer Systems Design Services is the leading industry with $33.3M, followed by Janitorial Services with $20.9M and Facilities Support Services with $18.2M."
      }
